session 27 amendment: the 27A queries are written by a model as a simulated searcher (data/simq_s11.jsonl), before any is scored

No person wrote queries: the author stopped at the first folder, whose documents were unreadable with every
digit hidden, and asked for synthetic queries. Six blind subagents (Claude Opus 5.5) wrote two queries for
each of 100 folders from what the tool shows (the subagent for F061 to F080 was refused by an automated
check before it ran). The prompt is data/simq_s11_prompt.txt. Scoring, gates, H27a to H27c and the track
rule stand as registered; the paper reports these as model-written queries.

